# Chanterelle scout, exploding: the top of the stem, from under the cap down to below the eyes. One of the fourteen pieces the chanterelle scout bursts into, each the scout (the
# chanterelle_scout part, so they follow its edits) intersected with a cell; the cells split all of space with no gap or overlap,
# so the pieces fit together exactly and together are the scout. The cell is in the scout's pale inner flesh, which shows on the
# cut faces.
#
# How space is cut: a plane through the top of the stem, where it flares into the funnel, takes the cap off. The cap is a Voronoi
# of six seeds (a middle low in the funnel, with the flared top of the stem in it, and five wedges of the wavy rim with the ridges
# under them). Below it, the chanterelle_scout_core part holds the stem and its foot clear of the floating eyes and hands: inside
# it the stem breaks under the eyes and above the foot, and the foot in two; outside it each eye and each hand is a piece of its
# own, whole. Low detail: debris lives a few seconds. The surface is shaded as the whole scout's (its thickness and occlusion
# measured on the scout), so the pieces put together look like the scout itself.
format 1
surface part=chanterelle_scout

Detail detail=0.5
    Intersection
        Part part=chanterelle_scout
        Material material=chanterelle_inner
            Intersection
                # Inside the core: the stem and its foot
                Part part=chanterelle_scout_core
                # Below the cut under the cap
                Plane normal=(0.025, 0.9995, -0.02) height=-1.1494
                # Above the break under the eyes
                Plane normal=(0.1002, -0.9917, -0.0801) height=0.714
